@startuml logger-sequence
title Log record sequence — producer enqueue, then backend format and write

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

box "Producer thread" #FEFEFE
  actor "Call site" as Call
  participant "log / logAt" as Api
  participant "Logger" as Log
end box

participant "Ring" as Ring

box "Backend thread" #FEFEFE
  participant "Backend\n(jthread)" as Back
  participant "Sinks" as Sinks
end box

participant "ConsoleSink" as Con

== Filter (producer, no capture) ==

Call -> Api: info / log / fatal(category, fmt, args)
note right of Api
  Helpers compile out when the severity
  is below VISCERA_LOG_MIN_LEVEL.
  log() / logAt() still compare at runtime.
end note

Api -> Api: isBelowFloor(level)?
opt below compile-time floor
  Api --> Call: return
end

opt Fatal
  Api -> Log: sample timestamp, thread id, frame
  Api -> Api: formatFullLine() into 1024-byte stack buffer
  Api -> Log: tryWriteFatalConsole(line)
  Log -> Con: tryWriteFatal()  (try_lock, no wait)
  Con --> Log: consoleWritten
end

Api -> Log: loggerRunning()?
opt not running
  Log -> Log: count notRunning
  Api --> Call: return
end

Api -> Log: shouldLog(level, category)?
opt filtered out
  Api --> Call: return
end

opt not Fatal
  Api -> Log: sample timestamp, thread id, frame
end

== Capture and enqueue (producer, no sink I/O) ==

Api -> Log: enqueueLog(...)
Log -> Log: measureArgs() against 256-byte payload
opt argument pack does not fit
  Log -> Log: count argumentBudget
  Api --> Call: return
end

Log -> Ring: lock mutex
opt lock failed, not running, or ring full
  Log -> Log: count overflow or notRunning
  Log -> Ring: unlock
  Api --> Call: return
end

Ring --> Log: writeSlot()  (unpublished)
Log -> Log: fill Record header (kind = Log)
Log -> Log: storeArgs() into payload
opt storeArgs failed
  Log -> Log: destroyPack() if non-trivial
  Log -> Log: count argumentBudget
  Log -> Ring: abortLogSlot()  (unlock, do not publish)
  Api --> Call: return
end

Log -> Log: install formatThunk / destroyThunk
Log -> Ring: publish()
Log -> Ring: unlock
Log -> Ring: notifyOne()
Api --> Call: return
note over Call, Ring
  The producer is done. Formatting and sink I/O
  run on the backend; they are not on this call stack.
end note

== Backend (one loop iteration; mutex not held across format or I/O) ==

Back -> Ring: wait until not empty / stop / abandon / flush

alt abandon (flush or shutdown timed out)
  Back -> Ring: destroy remaining slots,\ndiscard AddSink unique_ptrs
  Back -> Sinks: flush()
  Back -> Back: completeFlush(); exit
else ring empty and stopping
  Back -> Sinks: flush()
  Back -> Back: completeFlush(); exit
else Kind = AddSink
  Back -> Ring: readSlot(); unlock
  Back -> Log: registerSink(controlSink)
  Back -> Ring: lock, consume(), unlock
else Kind = Log
  Back -> Ring: readSlot()  (slot stays occupied)
  Back -> Ring: unlock
  Back -> Back: format header + formatThunk()\ninto growable buffer
  note right of Back
    On format throw or buffer growth failure:
    count formattingFailures and emit
    "[file:line] formatting failed".
  end note
  Back -> Ring: lock
  Back -> Back: destroyThunk() if non-null
  Back -> Ring: consume()
  Back -> Ring: unlock
  Back -> Sinks: write(level, line)
  note right of Sinks
    Skip ConsoleSink when kFlagConsoleWritten
    is set (Fatal already printed on stderr).
    Three consecutive write failures disable
    that sink. Queue mutex is not held here.
  end note
  Back -> Sinks: emitOverflowSummary if overflow advanced
end

@enduml
